  "id": "federal-spending-by-state-fy2024",
  "about": "How much federal money reaches each of the 56 places per resident, relative to the national per-resident amount, for each federal budget line the game uses. 1.0 is the national average. A member of Congress weighs their state's stake when voting to raise or cut a line.",
  "retrievedAt": "2026-10-14",
  "stakeDefinition": "(place dollars / place population) / (national dollars / national population), national being the 56 places together, rounded to 3 decimals",
  "caveats": "Place of performance is where USAspending records the work or payment landing; grants to a state agency land in that state, and some contract dollars land at a headquarters rather than where the benefit is felt. Transaction obligations in fiscal year 2024, not outlays. Budget-function mapping is by agency and assistance listing, an approximation of OMB budget functions, not the Treasury's function table. Loans and insurance are excluded.",
  "method": {
    "nationalDefense": "USAspending spending_by_geography, place of performance by state, fiscal year 2024, contracts A-D, grants 02-05, direct payments 06 and 10, other 09 and 11. Department of Defense, all contracts, grants, direct payments and other assistance. Components: + Department of Defense ($426.5B). National total $426.5B over 343,734,883 residents.",
    "internationalAffairs": "USAspending spending_by_geography, place of performance by state, fiscal year 2024, contracts A-D, grants 02-05, direct payments 06 and 10, other 09 and 11. Department of State, USAID, Peace Corps, Millennium Challenge Corporation, Inter-American Foundation, African Development Foundation, Trade and Development Agency. Components: + Department of State ($6.4B); + Agency for International Development ($4.5B); + Peace Corps ($0.0B); + Millennium Challenge Corporation ($0.1B); + Inter-American Foundation ($0.0B); + African Development Foundation ($0.0B); + United States Trade and Development Agency ($0.0B). National total $11.1B over 343,734,883 residents. Places with no recorded dollars on this line (stake 0): PR, GU, VI, AS, MP.",
    "naturalResources": "USAspending spending_by_geography, place of performance by state, fiscal year 2024, contracts A-D, grants 02-05, direct payments 06 and 10, other 09 and 11. Department of the Interior, Environmental Protection Agency, Corps of Engineers Civil Works, USDA Forest Service. Components: + Interior ($19.6B); + EPA ($46.7B); + Corps of Engineers Civil Works ($0.0B); + Forest Service ($6.7B). National total $73.0B over 343,734,883 residents.",
    "agriculture": "USAspending spending_by_geography, place of performance by state, fiscal year 2024, contracts A-D, grants 02-05, direct payments 06 and 10, other 09 and 11. Department of Agriculture, less Food and Nutrition Service (income security) and Forest Service (natural resources). Components: + USDA ($169.7B); - less Food and Nutrition Service ($132.2B); - less Forest Service ($6.7B). National total $30.8B over 343,734,883 residents.",
    "transportation": "USAspending spending_by_geography, place of performance by state, fiscal year 2024, contracts A-D, grants 02-05, direct payments 06 and 10, other 09 and 11. Department of Transportation. Components: + Department of Transportation ($114.2B). National total $114.2B over 343,734,883 residents.",
    "communityAndRegionalDevelopment": "USAspending spending_by_geography, place of performance by state, fiscal year 2024, contracts A-D, grants 02-05, direct payments 06 and 10, other 09 and 11. FEMA, Small Business Administration, Economic Development Administration, Appalachian Regional Commission, Delta Regional Authority, HUD community development block grant programs. Components: + FEMA ($40.9B); + SBA ($0.7B); + EDA ($1.0B); + ARC ($0.2B); + DRA ($0.1B); + HUD CDBG programs 14.218, 14.228, 14.239, 14.248, 14.255, 14.256 ($8.4B). National total $51.2B over 343,734,883 residents.",
    "education": "USAspending spending_by_geography, place of performance by state, fiscal year 2024, contracts A-D, grants 02-05, direct payments 06 and 10, other 09 and 11. Department of Education plus Department of Labor, less unemployment insurance (income security). Components: + Department of Education ($92.3B); + Department of Labor ($10.5B); - less unemployment insurance 17.225 ($3.0B). National total $99.7B over 343,734,883 residents.",
    "health": "USAspending spending_by_geography, place of performance by state, fiscal year 2024, contracts A-D, grants 02-05, direct payments 06 and 10, other 09 and 11. Department of Health and Human Services (Medicaid 93.778, NIH, CDC, HRSA and the rest), less ACF (income security) and the Medicare programs. Components: + HHS ($1844.8B); - less ACF ($69.3B); - less Medicare programs 93.770, 93.773, 93.774 ($1029.4B). National total $746.1B over 343,734,883 residents.",
    "medicare": "CMS Medicare Geographic Variation by National, State and County, 2023, state level: actual payment per fee-for-service beneficiary (TOT_MDCR_PYMT_PC) times all beneficiaries including Medicare Advantage (BENES_TOTAL_CNT); USAspending carries Medicare in only a few places and was not used. URL https://data.cms.gov/data-api/v1/dataset/6219697b-8f6c-4164-bed4-cd9317c58ebc/data?filter%5BYEAR%5D=2023&filter%5BBENE_GEO_LVL%5D=State&filter%5BBENE_AGE_LVL%5D=All&size=100. National $879.7B over 343,484,008 residents of the 53 places the source covers. ESTIMATED stake 1 (national average) for GU, AS, MP: the source does not report them.",
